DESCRIPTION:Organizer: OCPL - Aliso Viejo Branch\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60
  months\\nCategory: Arts & Crafts\\n\\nJoin us for a doubleheader event fe
 aturing: \n\nDucks Gaming Lounge | Outdoor Hockey Rink | Slapshot Lanes | 
 Games & Music & Crafts | Author/Illustrator Talks | Registration for the W
 inter Reading Program | Wild Wing Meet-And-Greets\n\nDon't miss this excit
 ing lineup with fun for the whole family!\n\n4:30-6:00 pm: Anaheim Ducks F
 aceoff Activities\n6:00 pm: Meet Author Mary Shaw (complimentary books ava
 ilable while supplies last)\n\nMary Shaw is a Waterloo\, Ontario native bu
 t spends summers at her cottage outside of Ottawa. Mary is a mother of thr
 ee - Taylore\, Brady\, and Caroline. She credits them - and their sporting
  adventures\, for swaing her into writing children's books. Her son\, Brad
 y\, an avid hocky player\, is in inspiration for BRADY BRADY. Her oldest\,
  Taylore\, is the inspiration for 'Tes' in the 'Twirling Torpedo'. In addi
 tion to writing\, Mary is an active volunteer in the animal rescue communi
 ty.\n\nLearn more at libraries.oc.gov/winter-reading-challenge\\n\\nMore i
 nfo: https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/18029881
LOCATION:Aliso Viejo\, Aliso Viejo
URL:https://ocpl.libcal.com/event/18029881
