BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Holiday Festival of Lights
DTSTART;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T100000
DTEND;TZID=America/Los_Angeles:20261219T100000
DTSTAMP:20261122T160111Z
UID:54170e378e7d8388646487f42d9b8518@family-events-agent
SEQUENCE:0
CATEGORIES:children,play,toddler,museum,family
DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Pretend City Children's Museum - Events\\nAges: 0-6
 0 months\\nCategory: Music & Dance\\n\\nLight up the holiday season at Pre
 tend City! Take a picture with Santa\, sing along to holiday tunes\, celeb
 rate Hanukkah\, and dance to West African drums.\n10am-11pm: Pictures with
  Santa \n11am-11:30am: Holiday Tunes with OCSA Thespian Songbirds \n1pm:
  Celebrating Hanukkah\n2:30pm: Music and Movement with Fouta Toro West Afr
 ican Dance and Drum Ensemble presented by Segerstrom Center for the Arts.
 \nSpace is limited! Book your tickets now\; this program is included in mu
 seum admission. \nDisclaimer: Events and dates are subject to change\nAbo
 ut the play partners:\nOCSA Thespian Songbirds\nThe Thespian Songbirds are
  an outreach performance group within our school&#8217\;s Thespian troupe.
  They regularly visit neighboring elementary schools to lead rhythm- and m
 usic-based educational activities for students. Troupe #6826 is Orange Cou
 nty School of the Arts&#8217\; chapter of the International Thespian Socie
 ty.\n&nbsp\;\nFouta Toro West African Dance and Drum Ensemble\nDirected by
  Malik Sow\, Fouta Toro West African Dance and Drum Ensemble presents the 
 dances\, songs\, and music of Senegal\, Mali\, and Guinea. Malik establish
 ed the group in 1992\, lending the name of his Fulani tribe to the dance e
 nsemble as a gesture of pride. The group aims to provide students with a c
 olorfully-costumed look at the history\, nations\, and people of the West 
 African region.\n&nbsp\;\nSegerstrom Arts Teach\nArts Teach is an educatio
 n program by Segerstrom Center for the Arts that offers assembly performan
